What comes from ModelTrace:

  lib/fingerprint.mjs   A JavaScript port of ModelTrace's fingerprint.py:
                        the number parser, the Hellinger and ordered-block
                        features, the nuisance-direction projection, the
                        standardisation, the cross-validated softmax
                        temperature and the family roll-up. test/fingerprint.test.mjs
                        holds it to fingerprint.py's own answers, computed by
                        test/parity/check.py.
  lib/challenges.mjs    The three random-number challenges, ported from
                        ModelTrace's generate_challenges(), wording unchanged:
                        the fingerprint only means something against prompts
                        shaped the way its reference data was collected.
  data/unified_bank.json
                        A copy of ModelTrace's data/unified_bank.json at the
                        time of writing: the model centroids, their scales,
                        the nuisance bases and the calibration temperatures.
                        Everything the monitor scores is scored against it.

ModelTrace itself builds on hanlinwenyuan/hlwy-ai-checker, which first used a
language model's random-number bias to check a third-party channel.

The magpie plugin API, the X-Magpie-Account header and `magpie provider pool`
are magpie's: https://github.com/yetone/magpie (MIT).
